vendor/zbar-wasm/
-----------------

A verbatim, unmodified copy of @undecaf/zbar-wasm version 0.11.0:

    https://github.com/undecaf/zbar-wasm
    https://www.npmjs.com/package/@undecaf/zbar-wasm

Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later. The full text is at vendor/zbar-wasm/LICENSE.
It wraps the ZBar barcode reader (https://github.com/mchehab/zbar), also
LGPL-2.1-or-later.

How it is used, and why that matters for the licence:

  * The files are byte-for-byte upstream. Nothing in them has been edited;
    CI re-downloads the published tarball and compares.
  * liboff loads it as a separate module at runtime, via a dynamic import
    from src/scanner/decode.js. It is not bundled, inlined, minified with,
    or otherwise combined into liboff's own code.
  * Replacing it is a file swap: drop a different build of the same library
    into vendor/zbar-wasm/ keeping the filenames, or point the ZBAR_URL
    constant in src/scanner/decode.js elsewhere. Nothing else needs to
    change, and no other part of the app imports it.

This keeps the LGPL component separable and replaceable, as the licence
intends, while the rest of liboff remains MIT.

Reproducing the vendored files:

    npm pack @undecaf/zbar-wasm@0.11.0
    tar xzf undecaf-zbar-wasm-0.11.0.tgz
    cp package/dist/index.mjs   vendor/zbar-wasm/
    cp package/dist/index.d.ts  vendor/zbar-wasm/
    cp package/dist/zbar.wasm   vendor/zbar-wasm/
    cp package/LICENSE          vendor/zbar-wasm/

Data sources
------------

Book metadata and cover images are fetched at runtime from Open Library
(https://openlibrary.org) and Google Books
(https://developers.google.com/books). No data is redistributed with this
repository; nothing is sent to them but an ISBN or a search string.
